What is the JavaScript to scroll to the top when a button/link/etc. is clicked?

Here's how to scroll to the top of a page when an element is clicked:

```javascript
// Method 1: Using window.scrollTo with smooth scrolling
document.getElementById('myButton').addEventListener('click', function() {
  window.scrollTo({
    top: 0,
    behavior: 'smooth' // For smooth scrolling animation
  });
});

// Method 2: Using window.scrollTo without animation
document.getElementById('myButton').addEventListener('click', function() {
  window.scrollTo(0, 0);
});

// Method 3: Using jQuery (if you're using jQuery)
$('#myButton').click(function() {
  $('html, body').animate({scrollTop: 0}, 'slow');
});
```

You can also use this with an anchor tag:
```html
<a href="#" onclick="window.scrollTo({top: 0, behavior: 'smooth'}); return false;">Back to Top</a>
```

Or with a button:
```html
<button onclick="window.scrollTo({top: 0, behavior: 'smooth'});">Back to Top</button>
```
